abstract: >-
  A dependency-free Python library and language-neutral conformance suite for
  making AI-assisted work checkable: a model's output is treated as a claim,
  a deterministic engine (the Lean kernel, a re-executed computation, an
  arithmetic reconciler) must confirm it, a human signs the exact bytes, and
  every step is hash-chained. Wedges cover ledgers, Lean proofs, manuscript
  claims, paper reproductions, a quantitative-hallucination benchmark, and
  peer-review provenance. Byte-compatible with the @kernel.chat/kbot-finance
  reference; conformance is proved by vectors, not prose.
